---
import AssetGrid from '../components/AssetGrid.astro';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import WorkDetails from '../components/WorkDetails.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
import { SuperHi, Vercel, Lyncxs, Freelance } from '../content/work-details';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang='en'>
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <aside class='work-in-progress'>
        This website is a work in progress. <a href='/blog/dip'
          >Take a look at my process</a
        >.
      </aside>
      <h1>Charles <span class='ital'>de Mount</span> Yahouédéou</h1>
      <p>
        Hello! I'm Charles, a design-adjacent software developer with 5 years of
        experience who thrives on the creative and human side of technology. As
        a community-taught developer, I started my professional career in a
        microbiology lab, but that scientific curiosity is exactly what drives
        me to understand how people interact with software. I've last worked at
        <a href='https://superhi.com' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>SuperHi</a>
        as a Senior Software Engineer.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm passionate about crafting intuitive and beautiful user interfaces
        that don't just work, but feel effortless. This passion has led me
        through high-growth startups like SuperHi and <a
          href='https://vercel.com'
          target='_blank'
          rel='noopener'>Vercel</a
        >, where I've focused on turning complex problems into interactive and
        accessible solutions while earning multiple design awards.
      </p>
      <section class='work-details'>
        <h2>I've worked at</h2>
        <WorkDetails {...SuperHi} isOpen />
        <WorkDetails {...Vercel} />
        <WorkDetails {...Lyncxs} />
        <WorkDetails {...Freelance} />
      </section>
      <section class='personal-projects'>
        <h2>I've built</h2>
        <ul class='personal-projects-list'>
          <li>
            <div>
              <h3>Raynab: An AI powered extension for YNAB</h3>
              <p>
                <a
                  href='https://www.raycast.com/CodetaroMiura/raynab'
                  target='_blank'
                  rel='noopener'>Raynab</a
                > is an AI powered extension for <a
                  href='https://www.ynab.com/'
                  target='_blank'
                  rel='noopener'>YNAB</a
                >, a personal finance app. It uses AI to help you manage your
                finances, and to generate reports and insights. I built it using
                React, TypeScript, and the YNAB API.
              </p>
              <AssetGrid
                assets={[
                  { type: 'image', url: 'raynab-1.webp' },
                  { type: 'image', url: 'raynab-2.webp' },
                  { type: 'image', url: 'raynab-3.webp' },
                  { type: 'image', url: 'raynab-4.webp' },
                ]}
                caption='Raynab in action'
              />
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div>
              <h3>Enigma: A recreation of the Enigma machine</h3>
              <p>
                After watching the Imitation Game, I was inspired to build a
                recreation of the Enigma machine to understand its inner
                workings and test my knowledge of React.
                <a
                  href='https://github.com/gogocharli/enigma'
                  target='_blank'
                  rel='noopener'>Enigma</a
                > is a react-based version of the machine using useReducer to manage
                the state of the machine. The machine reliably encrypts and decrypts
                messages with the same settings as the original machine, including
                the various rotors, reflector, and plugboard.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class='recommendations'>
        <h2>What people say about me</h2>
        <ul class='recommendations-list'>
          <li>
            <blockquote
              cite='https://www.linkedin.com/in/charles-yahouedeou/details/recommendations/'
            >
              <p>
                I would highly recommend Charles to any team looking for a
                software engineer who goes beyond writing code — someone who
                truly understands how technology can create delightful,
                accessible and memorable experiences(<a
                  href='https://www.linkedin.com/in/charles-yahouedeou/details/recommendations/'
                  >&hellip;</a
                >)
              </p>
              <cite>&#8212;Panna Nyeste</cite>, <cite
                >Head of Design at SuperHi</cite
              >
            </blockquote>
          </li>
          <li>
            <blockquote>
              <p>
                Charles is one of those rare colleagues who provides insightful
                feedback, champions customer pain points that need product
                improvement, and is a delight to work with. During my time
                working with him, he stood out as an empathetic communicator and
                excellent developer(<a
                  href='https://www.linkedin.com/in/charles-yahouedeou/details/recommendations/'
                  >&hellip;</a
                >)
              </p>
              <cite>&#8212;Juliet Jonak</cite>, <cite
                >Customer Success Manager at Vercel</cite
              >
            </blockquote>
          </li>
          <li>
            <blockquote>
              <p>
                Charles improved our whole engineering team with his
                initiatives. He implemented automated checks, high-quality
                testing, and better development practices. His technical skills,
                architectural thinking, and team commitment made him a talented
                developer. He is also one of the rare engineers who thinks about
                the return on investment and business needs for what they are
                working on, too(<a
                  href='https://www.linkedin.com/in/charles-yahouedeou/details/recommendations/'
                  >&hellip;</a
                >)
              </p>
              <cite>&#8212;Rik Lomas</cite>, <cite>CEO at SuperHi</cite>
            </blockquote>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>
    <aside class='shader-container'>
      <canvas id='shader'></canvas>
    </aside>
    <style>
      body {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: row;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
      }

      main {
        background-color: var(--color-white);
        max-width: unset;
        padding: 2em 2em 0;
        margin-block-end: 1em;
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
      }

      .work-in-progress {
        background-color: var(--color-jasmine-200);
        padding: 1rem;
        border-radius: 6px;
      }
      .work-in-progress a {
        color: var(--color-black);
      }
      .work-in-progress a:hover {
        background-color: inherit;
      }

      .shader-container {
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        z-index: -1;
        height: 100vh;
      }
      @media (min-width: 768px) {
        body {
          display: flex;
          flex-direction: row;
        }

        main {
          flex: 1 1 40%;
        }

        .shader-container {
          flex: 1 1 60%;
          position: sticky;
          top: 0;
          max-height: 100vh;
          overflow: hidden;
        }
      }

      .ital {
        font-style: italic;
      }

      .circled {
        font-feature-settings: 'ss03';
        font-size: 1.6rem;
        color: var(--color-amethyst-400);
        line-height: 1;
      }

      h2 {
        /* font-size: 1.25rem; */
        font-variation-settings:
          'wght' 400,
          'ital' 1;
        text-decoration: underline;
      }

      h3 {
        font-variation-settings:
          'wght' 600,
          'ital' 0;
      }

      .personal-projects-list {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 1.25rem;
      }
      .recommendations-list {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 1rem;
        list-style: none;
      }

      .recommendations-list li {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 1em 2em;
        border: 2px dashed var(--color-neutral-300);
        border-radius: 1rem;
      }
    </style>
    <script src='../shader.ts'></script>
  </body>
</html>
